OL,3,APokemon fans prepare for 'biggest day
OL,4,Ain a decade'
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor most people, Wednesday will be just
OL,7,Fanother day - the midweek hump at
OL,8,Fschool or work. But not for Pokemon
OL,9,Ffans.
OL,11,FThe Japanese brand has become one of
OL,12,Fthe most recognisable in the world,
OL,13,Fwith its colourful creatures appearing
OL,14,Fin video games and on shop shelves
OL,15,Facross the globe.
OL,17,FBut perhaps most synonymous with the
OL,18,FPokemon phenomenon is its trading card
OL,19,Fgame, which has been played, bought and
OL,20,Fsold between collectors for the last
OL,21,Fthree decades.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,170,160,200,105,0,100
